#   -g, --gaps            Dump the gap results from RADOS object contents. All other options are ignore ( except -j )
#   -i INFLIGHT, --inflight INFLIGHT
#                         Maximum number of in-flight ops to allow without a response. Default: 15000
#   -l LISTFILE, --listfile LISTFILE
#                         Optional: Bucket list file, should be one bucket name per line.
#   -m MATCH, --match MATCH
#                         Specify a prefix match for the object names. Only objects matching this prefix will be checked for gaps.
#   -n, --norandom        By default, the script randomizes the list of buckets before processing. On large bucket count environments, this may cause significant delay before start of processing due to
#                         the way the randomizing occurs. Set '-n' to Not Randomize the list to remove this delay.
#   --namespace NAMESPACE
#                         What namespace to use for sync / results objects. Default: rgw-gap-list
#   -p POOL, --pool POOL  Bucket Data Pool(s), default 'default.rgw.buckets.data default.rgw.buckets.non-ec', quoted space separated list is supported.
#   -s SYNCPOOL, --syncpool SYNCPOOL
#                         Synchronization / Queuing pool for the script ot use, default 'default.rgw.buckets.index'.
#   -r, --report          Generate bucket scrub metadata report.
#   -j, --json            Use JSON format for bucket scrub metadata report. Only considered with -g, -r and -x
#   -v, --verbosity       Optional: Verbosity level, multiple -v's are supported for higher verbosity, example: -vvv
#   -x, --verify          Used to verify the results from a prior run.
